      'Compare your plan with actual spending at the end of each month. The gaps show which numbers need adjusting — they don\'t mean budgeting failed.',
      'Housing is usually the largest expense. A common guideline is to keep rent or a mortgage near 30% of gross income or less, though local costs vary widely.',
      'For categories you tend to overspend in, like dining out, a separate card or envelope of cash gives you a hard stop when that money is gone.',
      'When you get a raise, decide how much goes to savings or debt before your spending quietly adjusts to the new income.',
