      'Work out your bare-bones monthly budget — essentials only — to know what your emergency fund truly needs to cover.',
      'Self-employed people and commission earners often keep a larger emergency fund because income can drop without warning.',
      'Review your emergency fund target once a year, or whenever your rent, household size or job changes.',
      'Keep a short written plan of what you\'d cut first if your income stopped. A plan makes an emergency fund last longer.',
      'Car repairs are one of the most common emergencies. A small monthly amount for maintenance keeps routine repairs from draining your emergency fund.',
