      'Interest on an emergency fund is a bonus, not the goal. Safety and quick access matter more than the rate.',
      'Two-income households can test their plan: how many months could one income plus savings cover essentials if the other income stopped?',
      'Job loss is a common emergency. Knowing how unemployment benefits work where you live, and how long they take to start, helps you size your fund.',
      'Available credit is not an emergency fund. Credit limits can be lowered, and borrowing adds interest to an already hard situation.',
      'Put unexpected money — a rebate, a gift, something you sold — toward your emergency fund until it reaches its target.',
      'Some people keep a small amount of cash at home for power or network outages, when cards and phones may not work.',
      'An emergency fund protects your other goals. Without one, surprises tend to get paid from retirement savings or goal money.',
      'Decide in writing what counts as an emergency for your household before one happens, so the choice isn\'t made under stress.',
