      'Small rate differences matter on big loans. On a 30-year, $250,000 mortgage, one percentage point can change total interest by roughly $50,000 or more.',
      'A longer loan term lowers the monthly payment but usually increases the total interest you pay.',
      'On most installment loans, early payments go mostly to interest. Extra principal paid early in the loan saves the most interest.',
