      'Over decades, inflation is a real risk for cash. Investing part of long-term savings can help money keep its buying power.',
      'Bond funds can lose value when interest rates rise. Shorter-term bond funds usually move less than long-term ones.',
      'To gauge your risk tolerance, ask how you\'d react to a 30% drop. If you\'d sell, your mix may be too aggressive for you.',
      'Speculative assets can swing wildly in value. Many investors limit them to a small amount they could afford to lose.',
      'Protection against a brokerage firm failing is not the same as protection against investment losses.',
      'Review investment statements for fees, contributions and allocation every few months, not every day. Checking constantly can encourage emotional decisions.',
      'You can start investing with small amounts. Many funds and accounts now have low or no minimums.',
